language ESSENCE' 1.0

$ Simple X-Sums Sudoku for demystify demo
$ Uses a standard cyclic sudoku solution with x-sums clues from all four sides.
$ Solution:
$  1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
$  4 5 6 7 8 9 1 2 3
$  7 8 9 1 2 3 4 5 6
$  2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 1
$  5 6 7 8 9 1 2 3 4
$  8 9 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
$  3 4 5 6 7 8 9 1 2
$  6 7 8 9 1 2 3 4 5
$  9 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8

$ side_labels[1,..] left clues (from left, one per row)
$ side_labels[2,..] top clues (from top, one per col)
$ side_labels[3,..] right clues (from right, one per row)
$ side_labels[4,..] bottom clues (from bottom, one per col)
$
$ Computed from the solution above:
$  Left: X=first cell of row, sum first X cells
$   Row 1: X=1 → 1
$   Row 2: X=4 → 4+5+6+7=22
$   Row 3: X=7 → 7+8+9+1+2+3+4=34
$   Row 4: X=2 → 2+3=5
$   Row 5: X=5 → 5+6+7+8+9=35
$   Row 6: X=8 → 8+9+1+2+3+4+5+6=38
$   Row 7: X=3 → 3+4+5=12
$   Row 8: X=6 → 6+7+8+9+1+2=33
$   Row 9: X=9 → 45
$  Top: X=first cell of column
$   Col 1: X=1 → 1
$   Col 2: X=2 → 2+5=7
$   Col 3: X=3 → 3+6+9=18
$   Col 4: X=4 → 4+7+1+5=17
$   Col 5: X=5 → 5+8+2+6+9=30
$   Col 6: X=6 → 6+9+3+7+1+4=30
$   Col 7: X=7 → 7+1+4+8+2+5+9=36
$   Col 8: X=8 → 8+2+5+9+3+6+1+4=38
$   Col 9: X=9 → 45
$  Right: X=last cell of row (reversed row)
$   Row 1: reversed [9,8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1] X=9 → 45
$   Row 2: reversed [3,2,1,9,8,7,6,5,4] X=3 → 3+2+1=6
$   Row 3: reversed [6,5,4,3,2,1,9,8,7] X=6 → 6+5+4+3+2+1=21
$   Row 4: reversed [1,9,8,7,6,5,4,3,2] X=1 → 1
$   Row 5: reversed [4,3,2,1,9,8,7,6,5] X=4 → 4+3+2+1=10
$   Row 6: reversed [7,6,5,4,3,2,1,9,8] X=7 → 7+6+5+4+3+2+1=28
$   Row 7: reversed [2,1,9,8,7,6,5,4,3] X=2 → 2+1=3
$   Row 8: reversed [5,4,3,2,1,9,8,7,6] X=5 → 5+4+3+2+1=15
$   Row 9: reversed [8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1,9] X=8 → 8+7+6+5+4+3+2+1=36
$  Bottom: X=last cell of column (reversed col)
$   Col 1: reversed col [9,6,3,8,5,2,7,4,1] X=9 → 45
$   Col 2: reversed col [1,7,4,9,6,3,8,5,2] X=1 → 1
$   Col 3: reversed col [2,8,5,1,7,4,9,6,3] X=2 → 2+8=10
$   Col 4: reversed col [3,9,6,2,8,5,1,7,4] X=3 → 3+9+6=18
$   Col 5: reversed col [4,1,7,3,9,6,2,8,5] X=4 → 4+1+7+3=15
$   Col 6: reversed col [5,2,8,4,1,7,3,9,6] X=5 → 5+2+8+4+1=20
$   Col 7: reversed col [6,3,9,5,2,8,4,1,7] X=6 → 6+3+9+5+2+8=33
$   Col 8: reversed col [7,4,1,6,3,9,5,2,8] X=7 → 7+4+1+6+3+9+5=35
$   Col 9: reversed col [8,5,2,7,4,1,6,3,9] X=8 → 8+5+2+7+4+1+6+3=36

